src/driver/*/captured/*.server.raw are test fixtures: the bytes the test servers sent, recorded once and
replayed by the tests. What PostgreSQL and MySQL wrote there — their messages — is that server's project's,
under its own licence:

- PostgreSQL 17 — the PostgreSQL License
- MySQL 8.4 Community Server — GPL-2.0, with Oracle's exceptions

The Redis transcripts keep only what the driver reads: each `COMMAND INFO` entry is cut to its six classic
fields (name, arity, flags, first key, last key, step) by `without_redis_text` in src/driver/redis/wire/tests.rs,
so none of Redis's own text is in them.

The fixtures are only read by the plugin's tests; nothing of them is built into the plugin.
